<title>SPAIN: Bank of Spain seen checking peseta rates - dealers.</title>
<headline>Bank of Spain seen checking peseta rates - dealers.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Spain was checking peseta/mark rates when the Spanish currency was trading at around 84.10 versus the mark, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Bank of Spain itself declined to comment, as is its usual policy.</p>
<p>Yesterday the central bank was seen selling pesetas against German marks and the U.S. dollar after the peseta strengthened to break the 84.00 level for the first time since May.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
